From: ps5cemu <ps5cemu@localhost>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 16:17:34 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] PS5: a Wii Remote or Pro Controller is there only while its
 DualSense is

InputManager::get_wpad_controller, through which padscore answers every
question about channels 0-3, gives no controller for one whose mapped
DualSense the port says is not there (PS5Cemu_WpadPresent). The port sets
up players 2-4 as Pro Controllers whether anyone holds their DualSenses
or not, and padscore calls a game's connect and sampling callbacks for
every controller it is given, from the first 5 ms tick: three Pro
Controllers paired and on from boot, where a Wii U has none until one is
connected. Skylanders Giants reads through a null pointer in its
callback at that point and the app ends (PS5CEMU-HAR #29; Cemu's wiki has
it crash at startup with any controller other than the GamePad on a PC
too). A player who signs in later gets theirs then, reported connected as
Cemu reports a new one.
---
 src/input/InputManager.cpp | 15 +++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 15 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/input/InputManager.cpp b/src/input/InputManager.cpp
index a492742..663a65e 100644
--- a/src/input/InputManager.cpp
+++ b/src/input/InputManager.cpp
@@ -705,13 +705,28 @@ std::shared_ptr<VPADController> InputManager::get_vpad_controller(size_t index)
 	return std::dynamic_pointer_cast<VPADController>(m_vpad[index]);
 }
 
+#if defined(CEMU_PS5)
+// the port (PS5PadController.cpp): whether a player's DualSense the controller is mapped to is there
+bool PS5Cemu_WpadPresent(const EmulatedController& controller);
+#endif
+
 std::shared_ptr<WPADController> InputManager::get_wpad_controller(size_t index) const
 {
 	if (index >= m_wpad.size())
 		return {};
 
 	std::shared_lock lock(m_mutex);
+#if defined(CEMU_PS5)
+	// PS5: a Wii Remote or Pro Controller is there for the game only while its DualSense is, as on a
+	// Wii U one is only once paired and on (the port sets up players 2-4 whether or not anyone holds
+	// their controllers, and a game sees every one it is given from its first frame)
+	auto controller = std::dynamic_pointer_cast<WPADController>(m_wpad[index]);
+	if (controller && !PS5Cemu_WpadPresent(*controller))
+		return {};
+	return controller;
+#else
 	return std::dynamic_pointer_cast<WPADController>(m_wpad[index]);
+#endif
 }
 
 std::pair<size_t, size_t> InputManager::get_controller_count() const
